{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Crisis at the Restaurant"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": " I Can't Believe This!"}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Exchange information about unlikely events or fairly certain conditions that will be fulfilled in present, past or future  in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "First vs. Zero Conditional"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "The Zero Conditional is used to talk about what you usually do in real-life situations. The result of the condition is always true according to the initial situation. <br>You use the First Conditional with If clauses to exchange opinions about possible future outcomes."}, {"type": "text", "content": " The Zero Conditional is also called the  Present Real Conditional. It is used to talk a situation that is always true when a general condition is met. <br> <br>You use the structure: <br><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">If/when</span> \u2026 Simple Present, \u2026 Simple Present or Simple Present \u2026 <span class=\"strong\">if/when</span> \u2026 Simple Present.</span> <br> <br>Both <span class=\"italic\">if</span> and <span class=\"italic\">when</span> are used in the Present Real Conditional. Using <span class=\"italic\">if</span> suggests that something happens less frequently. Using <span class=\"italic\">when</span> suggests that something happens regularly. <br> <br>You use the First Conditional to say it's possible that you will or will not do something. In that condition, something else may, may not will or will not happen. The outcome is not in the present, but in the future. <br> <br>Structure: <br><span class=\"italic\">If + Present Simple \u2026 will + verb \u2026</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "When people feel threatened they act out.  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "When you take a breath, your heart opens and you listen without judgement. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "When you order something and the restaurant runs out of it, it's frustrating."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Expressing Purpose and Intention"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " Besides using linking clauses to express your purpose, you can use certain nouns or verbal phrases to state your intentions."}, {"type": "text", "content": " When you want to express purpose and intention, the following phrases and expressions can be used. <br> <br> <ul><li>Nouns/Verbal phrases <br><span class=\"italic\">To have +  high hopes of / no intention of / no thoughts of / half a mind to ...</span> <br><span class=\"italic\">To be + / toying with the idea ...</span></li><li>Prepositional phrases<br><span class=\"italic\">in the hopes of getting / with a view to getting / with the aim of getting ...</span> </li></ul>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I have no real intention of saying anything.  "}, {"type": "example", "content": " I think that the customer complained with the aim of hurting someone. "}, {"type": "example", "content": " I have half a mind to call him out."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to act out "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to behave in angry way "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: When people feel threatened they act out.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le01ob09aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about customer relations."}], "type": "target_word_de